1
00:04:43,333 --> 00:04:49,333
Something wicked this way hops.

2
00:09:26,666 --> 00:09:32,666
Wallace & Gromit: The Curse of the Were-Rabbit is a adventure,
animation, comedy film directed by Steve Box.

3
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:16,000
Cheese-loving eccentric Wallace and his cunning canine pal, Gromit, investigate a mystery in Nick Park's animated
adventure, in which the lovable inventor and his intrepid pup run a business ridding the town of garden pests.

4
00:18:53,333 --> 00:18:59,333
Using only humane methods that turn their home into a halfway house for evicted vermin, the pair stumble upon a
mystery involving a voracious vegetarian monster that threatens to ruin the annual veggie-growing contest.

5
00:23:36,666 --> 00:23:42,666
Wallace / Hutch (voice), played by Peter Sallis.

6
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:26,000
Victor Quartermaine (voice), played by Ralph Fiennes.

7
00:33:03,333 --> 00:33:09,333
Lady Campanula Tottington (voice), played by Helena Bonham Carter.

8
00:37:46,666 --> 00:37:52,666
PC Mackintosh (voice), played by Peter Kay.

9
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Reverend Clement Hedges (voice), played by Nicholas Smith.

10
00:47:13,333 --> 00:47:19,333
Mrs. Mulch (voice), played by Liz Smith.

11
00:51:56,666 --> 00:52:02,666
Wallace & Gromit: The Curse of the Were-Rabbit is a platform video game
developed by Frontier Developments and published by Konami.

12
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
It was released for the PlayStation 2 and Xbox consoles.

13
01:01:23,333 --> 01:01:29,333
It was released in 2005 in North America in September, Europe and Australia in October,
and in Japan the following year on 16 March 2006 for the PlayStation 2.

14
01:06:06,666 --> 01:06:12,666
It is based on the film of the same name by
DreamWorks Animation and Aardman Animations.

15
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:56,000
A version for the GameCube was also announced but was never released.

16
01:15:33,333 --> 01:15:39,333
The film explores themes of northern england,
hunter, competition, village, garden.

17
01:20:16,666 --> 01:20:22,666
The tone is lighthearted.
